// restart_transfer -- operation model §4, level: CONFIGURATION.
//
// completes_when: the channel's working registers have been reloaded with
//                 their originally programmed -- or last-fetched-descriptor --
//                 values.
// waits for:      nothing observable. Pin-only, asserted by construction.
//
// Configuration rather than end-to-end because nothing leaves the device; only
// internal state is restored. The canonical consumer is the Ethernet-MAC
// collision case in §3.10: a partially transmitted frame has to be resent from
// the beginning.
//
// Needs caps.ars on the channel and REST_EN set through the MMIO model, so
// this is one of the few places the two operation models have an ordering
// dependency on each other rather than merely running concurrently.
//
// open (§6): the spec requires "no transfer in progress" when dma_rest_i
//            asserts. That is a precondition, and deliberately not formalized
//            in this pass -- but it is the one case where violating it looks
//            destructive, which makes it the strongest candidate for the first
//            precondition work. Note the tension with blocking semantics: the
//            caller must know a concurrent transfer_single() is quiescent, and
//            no operation reports that.
import wb_dma_hs_pkg::*;

extend component wb_dma_hs_c {

    target function void restart_transfer() {
        wb_dma_hs_pulse_rest(chan);
    }
}
